# RIC — base rules

- Reply in **European Portuguese** (pt-PT). Keep rule files and code comments concise; prefer English identifiers in code.
- Read `CONTEXTO-PAP.md` before large changes. Update it when decisions change.
- System design source of truth for the rewrite: `docs/ARQUITETURA.md` (2026-10-25). Schedule: `docs/PLANEAMENTO.md` (P1-crono).
- PAP hardware default: recycled PC + touch screen on the same machine; UI on localhost (no Wi-Fi required for core).
- Target OS on the RIC machine: lightweight Linux (systemd + browser kiosk). Windows is optional for the student's dev PC only; runtime/demo target is Linux.
- Scope: school PAP MVP. Prefer simple, maintainable solutions over enterprise patterns.
- Priorities: interaction + privacy + hardware reuse. Locomotion/arms are later extras, not the critical path.
- Reminders = reliable local backend. LLM = conversation/company. Reminders must work without LLM and without internet.
- Never diagnose disease or prescribe medication. Reminders and logging only.
- Local-first: no sensitive data to cloud by default. Cloud LLM only if explicit and optional.
- Prefer reused hardware; justify any new purchase in docs.
- Do not invent features outside CONTEXTO scope without asking Pedro.
- Code docs: keep detailed per-file explanations in `docs/codigo/` in sync when code changes (see rule `50-explicacoes-codigo`).
